.TH "GOOBERS SERVICE" "1" "" "Goobers" "Goobers Manual"
.SH NAME
goobers service \- install and manage the platform-supervised daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgoobers service\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Usage: goobers service <subcommand> [path]

Install and manage the goobers daemon under the current platform's user
supervisor: systemd on Linux, launchd on macOS, or a per-user Scheduled Task
on Windows. The stable service host launches the instance's mutable
binary, receives the same graceful-shutdown trigger as a foreground daemon,
and owns validated self-update handoff, health checks, and rollback.

On Windows, `service install` is a separate machine-service path that runs as
LocalSystem and cannot inherit user-scoped CLI accounts, Credential Manager,
LOCALAPPDATA, mapped drives, or user PATH. It requires explicit acknowledgement.

Subcommands:
  install     install, enable, and start the service
  uninstall   gracefully stop, disable, and remove the service
  start       resume an installed-but-stopped service
  stop        halt the running service without disabling or removing it
  status      report whether the service is installed and running
  task-install     install a per-user Windows Scheduled Task
  task-uninstall   remove the per-user Windows Scheduled Task
  task-start       start the per-user Windows Scheduled Task
  task-stop        stop the per-user Windows Scheduled Task
  task-status      report Scheduled Task state and Windows identity

Run `goobers service install -h`, `goobers service uninstall -h`,
`goobers service start -h`, `goobers service stop -h`, or
`goobers service status -h` for details. Default path is ".".
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
goobers service install
goobers service status
goobers service uninstall
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgoobers\fR(1)
